# Fetched and built by `make kryoptic` — a second PKCS#11 module to test
# the provider against. Never committed: it is someone else's project, and
# the build is large.
.kryoptic/

# Token databases and configs created by `make token` and `make token-two`.
#
# A pattern, because .token2 was added the moment a suite needed TWO tokens
# and a named list would have missed it — the same gap the binaries below
# were switched to a pattern for.
.token*/

# Binaries.
#
# A pattern, not a list of names. The list form was forgotten in sessions
# 8, 9 and 10 — every time a suite was added, its binary showed up
# untracked — so the names are matched and the sources exempted instead.
#
# The lesson was only half applied: test_* became a pattern and the p11_
# binaries stayed a one-name list, so the first new one (p11_qualify,
# session 18) was untracked exactly as before. Both are patterns now.
test_*
!test_*.c
!test_*.h
p11_*
!p11_*.c
!p11_*.h

# Built by `make openssl` — OpenSSL 3.5, needed because Kryoptic gates
# eddsa on 3.2 and the post-quantum mechanisms on 3.5, and the distribution
# ships 3.0.
.openssl/
.openssl-src/
